{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>A land not in poverty, etc.</b> The meaning: for there are people who, although they are wealthy, conduct themselves in the manner of the poor, for two reasons: first, that they fear lest they collapse and become poor; therefore they scrimp in order not to spend much. Second, that they not satisfy themselves, so that it not be apparent that they are rich. Therefore he said <b>not in poverty</b>, etc. — that there is no place in it for the two aforementioned concerns, for both concerns arise through the existence of this one being rich and this one being poor, and through the existence of collapse, and neither of these exists in this land. And he gave a reason for this in saying <b>you will lack nothing in it</b> — meaning, granted if the wealth comes from the virtue of the land, this one strives and grows rich and this one does not strive and is poor; but since in the land [of Israel] the wealth is dependent [on the land itself], and the land enriches whoever is enriched from it and is distributed equally to all of them, if so they are all rich. Also there is no need to fear collapse all the time they are in the land, for from it [comes] wealth and possessions — and this is what he said <b>in it</b>:" "<b>And he mentioned</b> two specific things, which are iron and copper, which are two things fundamentally necessary for human needs. And after this he mentioned <b>and you will eat</b>, etc. — meaning, for there is no perfection to the land when it is praised for its fruits if it lacks things needed for the settlement of the city and the needs of people, for the praise would go to compensate for what is missing. And surely you will find many farmers of gardens and orchards who have much and much, and profit greatly from what the soil gives of its power in the produce of the land and the fruit of the tree, and even so they stand in want, for they spend everything on the needs of their necessities and their clothing. Therefore, after he said <b>a land of wheat</b>, etc., he concluded by saying <b>you will lack nothing in it</b> — and you do not need to export from the value of the land's fruits to another place in order to bring in their place things needed for human use and the use of his implements, and in this they are in the category of ״וְאָכַלְתָּ וְשָׂבָעְתָּ״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:04.498762998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}